	//
	// Asks the workspace's AI provider to draft an automation rule from one sentence in the caller's own words — "when a task is created in Website relaunch, give it to Lisa". Needs what writing a rule needs: the automation permission at the scope, and a plan that includes rules.
	// The draft uses only what this workspace offers: the triggers it serves, the conditions the rule editor composes, a fixed set of entry-level actions, and only the people, collections and labels the sentence names and the caller may read. A model writes no expression and no address; what it could not draft is listed in the payload's `not_drafted`.
