// DeleteRetentionPolicy Withdraw a retention rule
//
// The rule stops applying. What it already did stands - retention deletes, and a deletion is not undone by withdrawing the instruction that caused it - and what it had marked for a future pass is unmarked, because an entry counting down towards a rule nobody holds any more would be deleted by a rule that does not exist.
// Withdrawing one that is not there is not an error. Auditable.
//
// Corresponds with DELETE /retention-policies/{policyId} (the `DeleteRetentionPolicy` operationId).
