// RegisterOauthClientWithBodyWithResponse Register a third-party app
//
// A name, the exact redirect URIs it may be sent back to, and whether it can keep a secret. A public client - a native or single-page app - gets no secret and must bring PKCE to every authorization (RFC 7636); a confidential client gets one, in clear, for the only time, stored as a hash under its own purpose label.
// Redirect URIs match exactly, byte for byte: a prefix or wildcard match is how authorization codes end up on attacker-controlled pages.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
